* Simplified behavioural model of ONE TL072 amplifier, written for circuit-tutor.
* This is NOT the Texas Instruments vendor macro-model: single dominant pole, no slew-rate
* limit. Aol = 2e5 (106 dB), GBW = 3 MHz; output swings to about 1.5 V inside each rail.
* The output current is drawn from VCC when sourcing and returned to VEE when sinking, so supply
* currents and dissipation are right. Swing limits are diode clamps on the gain node, driven
* from ground-referenced copies of the rails: smooth, so the operating point converges directly.
* Pin order matches the registry unit_line: inp inm vcc vee out
.subckt TL072 inp inm vcc vee out
rin inp inm 1e12
cin inp inm 2p
* gain stage: 10 uA/V into 20 Gohm = 2e5, dominant pole at 15 Hz
g1 0 n1 inp inm 10u
r1 n1 0 20g
c1 n1 0 0.5305p
* clamps: n1 stays within about (VEE + 1.5 V, VCC - 1.5 V); 1.55 V = 1.5 V + the drop of a sharp (n = 0.1) diode
erhi rhi 0 vcc 0 1
vhi rhi nhi 1.55
dhi n1 nhi dclamp
erlo rlo 0 vee 0 1
vlo nlo rlo 1.55
dlo nlo n1 dclamp
* output stage
eout n2 0 n1 0 1
rout n2 n3 75
vsense n3 out 0
* move the output current onto the supply pins (smooth split, 1 uA rounding at zero load)
bsrc vcc 0 i = 0.5 * (i(vsense) + sqrt(i(vsense) * i(vsense) + 1e-12))
bsnk 0 vee i = 0.5 * (sqrt(i(vsense) * i(vsense) + 1e-12) - i(vsense))
* quiescent current, about 1.4 mA at +/-15 V
rq vcc vee 21.4k
.model dclamp d(is=1e-14 n=0.1)
.ends TL072
